 "verified_wiring_facts": [
  "V1 Warmup all-path persistence. The try/finally at qualification 55-64 covers the ready check, owner.check and capture_replay. prepare_capture returns refusals instead of raising (client 842-844). capture_replay settles every exception and re-raises non-Exception only after settling (client 882-886). A persist failure writes <name>.write-error.json and re-raises (qualification 15-22), which also handles sealed-B N1 (inf) fail-closed.",
  "V2 The warmup passes the original absolute D=owner.deadline and R=owner.reserve unchanged (qualification 59-60); drain = D-R, and truncation is refused (client 874-876).",
  "V3 S is never retimed: the client refuses a passed or too-far S (client 488-489, 734-735, 878-879), runtime.run refuses entry before S (runtime 599), and wait_for_start refuses a past S or out-of-envelope start (runtime 765-767).",
  "V4 One S binds everything: qualification 102 -> describe_protocol start_at (108) -> protocol sha -> permit protocol_sha256 (113) -> NominalRuntime start_at (124; enforced equal by _binding at runtime 336) -> run_episode offered_start (127).",
  "V5 The permit is re-validated at every authorization: identity labels, source/protocol sha, run_id and clock_domain against the snapshot and current clock_domain(), window/limits, snapshot age, budget set and command count (permit 55-104; runtime 462-477, 546-566). run_id is the actual post-warmup GET value (qualification 111).",
  "V6 The post-warmup gateway identity/clock_domain/cost_spec is checked against source-time expected values (qualification 96-99) and persisted redacted (100).",
  "V7 The output dir is fresh (smoke 227, mkdir without exist_ok), so there is no stale journal or episode resume.",
  "V8 The warmup outcome check reads the in-place envelope (client 863, 886-888); the status short-circuit avoids None records (client 678).",
  "V9 The admin key is per run (smoke 253) and redacted by services.write (smoke 44-45); the client sends/records no auth header (client 95-96); the runtime redacts bodies/errors (runtime 389, 630, 649).",
  "V10 Body exceptions are appended to errors and force lifecycle_passed=false (smoke 280-284, 323-326). KeyboardInterrupt/SystemExit are re-raised after report.json is written."
 ],
